WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.776
To get to know a system, such as a filter or a room, you send it a known test signal and compare what comes out with what went in.

2
00:00:08.178 --> 00:00:16.595
A sine measures one frequency at a time. A sweep goes through all of them: the output amplitude traces the filter's response over time.

3
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:29.446
An impulse contains every frequency at once. What comes out is the impulse response, and its spectrum is the filter's frequency response.

4
00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:39.780
Noise also contains every frequency; at the output, its spectrum traces the shape of the filter. It sounds more natural than an impulse, but you have to average because it is random.
